From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: az0x <dev@localhost>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:26:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: add the DSI panels fitted to inMusic AZ01

The 800x1280 DSI panel on inMusic AZ01 boards (Denon DJ Prime GO and
relatives). Nothing in-tree drives it, and without a drm_panel the whole
display pipeline stays down: rockchip-drm is component-based and will not
finish binding until every component registers, so there is no card0 at all
and X has no DRM device.

This driver sends no panel initialisation sequence, by design. u-boot already
brings the display up before handing over - the VOP reports "enabled by
bootloader" and the device tree carries a framebuffer reservation for the
handover - so the panel controller is configured by the time Linux probes.
prepare() therefore takes a reference on the supply and deliberately does not
touch the reset line, and the reset GPIO is claimed GPIOD_ASIS so that merely
requesting it cannot drive the panel out of the state u-boot left it in.

The mode is not guessed. It was read field for field off the running vendor
kernel with modetest:

  800x1280 60.06  800 877 901 925  1280 1292 1296 1314  73000  preferred

and the pixel clock independently confirmed as dclk_vop1 = 73000000.

The lane count is the one parameter recoverable neither from the device tree
nor from sysfs on the vendor kernel. Four is the arithmetic fit: 73 MHz at
24bpp is 1.752 Gbps, so 438 Mbps per lane over four, where two lanes would
demand 876 Mbps per lane.

Note the compatible. The shipped device tree names urt,umo-p076md-t, but
u-boot rewrites it: the panel actually fitted to this unit is a
umoh-9522md-t, which is what the vendor kernel binds. No vendor device tree in
the family declares that string at all.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor board support]

Carries initialisation sequences lifted verbatim from the vendor bootloader
for seven compatibles, with no datasheet behind them, and a mode table taken
from the same place. That provenance is not acceptable upstream as-is.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig                 |  13 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Makefile                |   1 +
 .../gpu/drm/panel/panel-urt-umoh-9522md-t.c   | 502 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 1450 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-urt-umoh-9522md-t.c

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig
index 3a2f4a9f1d46..eda216aad6a4 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig
@@ -788,6 +788,19 @@ config DRM_PANEL_TRULY_NT35597_WQXGA
 	  Say Y here if you want to enable support for Truly NT35597 WQXGA Dual DSI
 	  Video Mode panel
 
+config DRM_PANEL_URT_UMOH_9522MD_T
+	tristate "URT UMOH-9522MD-T DSI panel"
+	depends on OF
+	depends on DRM_MIPI_DSI
+	depends on BACKLIGHT_CLASS_DEVICE
+	help
+	  Say Y here to support the URT UMOH-9522MD-T 800x1280 MIPI-DSI panel
+	  fitted to inMusic AZ01 boards such as the Denon DJ Prime GO.
+
+	  The driver sends no initialisation sequence: u-boot brings the panel
+	  up before handing over, and this only supplies the mode so that the
+	  component-based rockchip-drm can finish binding.
+
 config DRM_PANEL_VISIONOX_RM69299
 	tristate "Visionox RM69299"
 	depends on OF
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Makefile b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Makefile
index 433e93d57949..8028ade613ac 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Makefile
@@ -80,6 +80,7 @@ obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_TPO_TD028TTEC1) += panel-tpo-td028ttec1.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_TPO_TD043MTEA1) += panel-tpo-td043mtea1.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_TPO_TPG110) += panel-tpo-tpg110.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_TRULY_NT35597_WQXGA) += panel-truly-nt35597.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_URT_UMOH_9522MD_T) += panel-urt-umoh-9522md-t.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_VISIONOX_RM69299) += panel-visionox-rm69299.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_VISIONOX_VTDR6130) += panel-visionox-vtdr6130.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_VISIONOX_R66451) += panel-visionox-r66451.o
