+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+/*
+ * URT UMOH-9522MD-T MIPI-DSI panel, as fitted to inMusic AZ01 boards
+ * (Denon DJ Prime GO and relatives).
+ *
+ * The panel is an ILI9881C-class controller: register banks are selected with
+ * a 0xFF 0x98 0x81 <page> long write and configured with DCS short writes.
+ *
+ * The initialisation sequence below is the vendor's, recovered from
+ * drivers/video/urt_umoh_9522md_t_panel.c inside U-Boot
+ * 2016.05-inmusic-20230621, dumped off the eMMC "uboot" partition of a
+ * Prime Go. It is reproduced byte for byte; nothing here was guessed.
+ *
+ * An earlier version of this driver sent no sequence at all and relied on
+ * u-boot having configured the panel before Linux started. That works from a
+ * cold boot and fails the moment anything powers the panel down: the supply,
+ * vcc-mipi, is regulator-boot-on but not regulator-always-on, so DRM blanking
+ * dropped it and the display never came back - backlight lit, no picture. With
+ * a real sequence the panel can be brought up from cold, which is what the
+ * reset pulse and the table below do.
+ *
+ * The mode is not guessed. It was read off the running vendor kernel with
+ * modetest, field for field:
+ *
+ *   800x1280 60.06  800 877 901 925  1280 1292 1296 1314  73000  preferred
+ *
+ * and the pixel clock independently confirmed as dclk_vop1 = 73000000.
+ *
+ * The lane count is the one parameter not recoverable from the device tree or
+ * from sysfs on the vendor kernel. Four is the arithmetic fit: 73 MHz x 24bpp
+ * = 1.752 Gbps, so 438 Mbps per lane over four. Two lanes would demand
+ * 876 Mbps per lane, which is unusual at this resolution. If the panel stays
+ * dark with the DSI host reporting link errors, two lanes is the fallback to
+ * try.
+ */
